{"op":"add","path":"/elements/why-annotation","value":{"type":"Annotation","props":{"icon":"trend","title":"Why This Month Stood Out","content":"The peak month combined an above-trend wave of new customer acquisitions with strong expansion from existing accounts upgrading or adding seats — while churn remained contained relative to inflows. This rare convergence of all three levers moving favorably at once produced the year's largest net MRR gain. The plan breakdown below shows which pricing tier drove the bulk of the spike.","severity":"info"},"children":[]}}
{"op":"add","path":"/elements/methodology-text","value":{"type":"TextBlock","props":{"content":"Monthly MRR changes were computed from subscription records grouped by calendar month. Net new MRR is the sum of new customer revenue plus expansion from existing accounts minus churned revenue. The peak month is identified as the month with the highest net new MRR total across all plans. The waterfall chart shows the three components that make up that month's gain. The plan breakdown reflects contributions from each pricing tier during the peak month only and is not affected by the plan filter — the monthly trend bar chart does update when a plan is selected.","variant":"body"},"children":[]}}
